    <!-- Mode onboarding scripts (chromeless tap-to-advance overlay) -->
    <string-array name="onboarding_trace">
        <item>This is Trace mode.</item>
        <item>Tap \'Open\' to add your first layer. Once it\'s in, pinch and drag on the canvas to size and place it.</item>
        <item>When they are where and how you want them, press the Freeze button to turn your phone into a lightbox for tracing onto paper.</item>
        <item>We recommend using either Trace mode or Mockup mode for editing.</item>
        <item>That way your imagery is all ready to go and your phone can focus on augmenting reality when you press the AR button.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="onboarding_ar">
        <item>AR Projection — projects your design onto a real wall using the phone\'s depth sensor and spatial tracking.</item>
        <item>Point at the wall and move slowly side-to-side. Coloured shapes appear as the engine maps the surface. Wait until the wall area is covered.</item>
        <item>Just tap the screen. The app photographs the wall, extracts tracking features, and locks the anchor instantly.</item>
        <item>Tap \'Open\' to add a design layer — it projects onto the wall using the anchor you just set.</item>
        <item>Tip — blank white walls, smooth concrete, and single-colour surfaces won\'t track. Aim your anchor point at graffiti, rough plaster, or any distinct mark.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="onboarding_overlay">
        <item>Live Overlay — your design floats over the live camera view, no surface scanning needed.</item>
        <item>Tap \'Open\' to add a layer — pick a photo and it appears here, floating over the live camera view.</item>
        <item>Pinch to scale, drag to reposition. The overlay stays fixed to your screen — step back to see how it fits the wall.</item>
    </string-array>
    <!-- Shown once on first launch on devices where ARCore is not supported. -->
    <string-array name="onboarding_ar_unavailable">
        <item>This device doesn\'t support ARCore, so the AR Projection mode isn\'t available.</item>
        <item>You can still use Trace, Mockup, and Live Overlay — every mode except AR works without ARCore.</item>
        <item>Tap to dismiss.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="onboarding_mockup">
        <item>Photo Mockup — preview your design on a photo before you ever pick up a brush.</item>
        <item>Tap \'Wall\' to choose or take a photo of your surface. Do this first!</item>
        <item>Tap \'Open\' to add a layer on top of the wall photo. Pinch and drag to size and position it.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="onboarding_design">
        <item>This is Design — your workspace. Whatever you build here carries over into every other mode.</item>
        <item>Tap \'Open\' to add your first layer — pick a photo from your gallery and it lands here as your artwork.</item>
        <item>Tap a layer to open its tools — grouped into Paint, Retouch, Adjust and Effects folders. Pinch and drag on the canvas to size and place it.</item>
        <item>When it looks right, choose how to use it: \'Trace\' to turn your phone into a lightbox, \'Mockup\' to preview on a photo, or \'AR\' to project it onto a wall.</item>
    </string-array>
